# um-texts 1
=== MATERIAL Adamantium
Adamantite
Very good material for making weapons and armor.

=== MATERIAL Bronze
Bronze
The cheapest and softest metal.

=== MATERIAL Burned_bones
Hard bone
Hard bone weapons can be made both sharper and stronger than tough bone ones.

=== MATERIAL Cotton
Cotton
Cotton is not much more expensive than rough fabric, but it does looks better.

=== MATERIAL Decayed_bones
Thin bone
This material is easy to get, but it is practically impossible to make decent weapons out of it.

=== MATERIAL Diamond
Diamond
Only the best craftsmen of the bygone race knew the secret of processing this material.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Black
Blue Dragon hide
Dragon hide makes strong leather armor, with good protection against lightning strikes.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Black_Bones
Blue Dragon bone
The perfect material for bone weapons! But it is not at all easy to obtain…

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Green
Green Dragon hide
Dragon hide makes strong leather armor, with good protection against acid.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Green_Bones
Green Dragon bone
Great for constructing bone weapons.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Red
Red Dragon hide
Dragon hide makes strong leather armor, with good protection against fire.

=== MATERIAL Dragon_Red_Bones
Red Dragon bone
A very good material for bone weapons.

=== MATERIAL Dry_bones
Tough bone
Tough bone weapons can be honed sharper than thin bone ones..

=== MATERIAL Granite
Granite
Heavier and nicer looking than ordinary stone. Makes better weapons, too.

=== MATERIAL Iron
Iron
Iron is better than bronze but inferior to other metals.

=== MATERIAL Malachite
Obsidian
The best material for stone weapons capable of carrying powerful spells.

=== MATERIAL Meteoric
Meteorite
The hardest of metals, the best material for weapons and armor.

=== MATERIAL Mithrill
Mithrill
Lightweight, very hard metal. Mithrill objects are capable of carrying strong spells.

=== MATERIAL Rock
Stone
Ordinary stone. Of course you can make weapons from it, but the quality would be rather poor.

=== MATERIAL Scrab_bones
Shell bones
Shell bone is not easy to come by. But the result is worth the effort!

=== MATERIAL Silicon
Silicon
A decent material for stone weapons.

=== MATERIAL Silk_Blue
Silk
This is a most expensive fabric, valued not only for its appearance, but also for its durability.

=== MATERIAL Silk_Red
Wool
Wool fabric is strong and can even absorb a blow  (though not very well).

=== MATERIAL Steel
Steel
Common steel.

=== MATERIAL Tanned_Thin
Hard leather
The best material for leather armor.

=== MATERIAL Thick
Tough leather
Common material for leather armor.

=== MATERIAL Thin
Thin leather
The flimsiest and weakest material for making leather armor. Use it only when nothing better is available.

=== MATERIAL Tiger_Hide
Tiger skin
Tiger skin is used for making beautiful and very hard armor.

=== MATERIAL Tiger_Hide_White
Snow Tiger skin
Snow Tiger skin is beautiful, strong, reliable... and expensive!

=== MATERIAL Troll_Black
Black Troll hide
Troll hide makes very strong leather armor.

=== MATERIAL Troll_Blue
Blue Troll hide
Troll hide makes very strong leather armor.

=== MATERIAL Troll_Green
Green Troll hide
Troll hide makes very strong leather armor.

=== MATERIAL Wool
Rough fabric
The cheapest fabric and lowest quality. Only very poor people wear such clothes.

